{"base_rate":0.5521796565389696,"brier":0.21784464993394975,"bss":0.11902683942357928,"bss_hi":0.24317847786005828,"bss_lo":-0.0068722448441850305,"chart":{"base":[539.3,213.7],"fp":[542.4,205.6],"lead":"62,133.3 272,136.9 482,132.2 692,104.4","note":{"base":"skill 0.12 — higher than 19% of cities","fp":"low end +21pp, high end +18pp","lead":"day-1 error 2.2 °C — better than 1% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 22%; promised 99% → rained 81%"},"rel":"63.4,372.2 190.6,321 498.3,212.6 682.7,117.3"},"country":"GB","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.1619286657859974,"ess":455.7437720847397,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Edinburgh</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Edinburgh rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>86%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>22%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nEDINBURGH: ROYAL BOTANIC GARDE, 1.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.12, ranked 176 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(133&ndash;191) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>22%</b></td><td class='num'>152</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>29%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'><b>38%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>59%</td><td class='num'><b>56%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>80%</td><td class='num'><b>61%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>94%</td><td class='num'><b>65%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>86%</b></td><td class='num'>231</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Edinburgh</b> <span class=\"muted\">United Kingdom</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;55% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 55% of days.</p><p>The forecast did only slightly better. The difference is within the margin of error.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.12</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>133&ndash;191\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Edinburgh &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Edinburgh\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" fo