" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 32%&amp;#10;It rained 38% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"171.75837837837838\" cy=\"244.27027027027026\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 59%&amp;#10;It rained 56% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"266.0104\" cy=\"178.15999999999997\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 80%&amp;#10;It rained 61% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"340.3032\" cy=\"158.74666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 94%&amp;#10;It rained 65% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"390.94880000000006\" cy=\"144.18666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 86% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 231 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.87740259740264\" cy=\"70.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(55%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Edinburgh the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.28) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.05).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>57%</td><td class='num'>-0.047</td><td class='num'>22.2%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>65%</td><td class='num'>-0.000</td><td class='num'>18.2%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>57%</td><td class='num'>0.117</td><td class='num'>17.1%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'>0.285</td><td class='num'>11.5%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":55.95206,"lon":-3.19648,"n":757,"n_cities":216,"name":"Edinburgh","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.022000000000000172,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0022368421052631577,"n":152,"obs":0.21710526315789475,"sig":true},{"hi":0.1960000000000008,"lo":0.022000000000000172,"mean":0.08853333333333334,"n":75,"obs":0.29333333333333333,"sig":true},{"hi":0.47,"lo":0.1960000000000008,"mean":0.32135135135135134,"n":74,"obs":0.3783783783783784,"sig":false},{"hi":0.71,"lo":0.47,"mean":0.5876000000000001,"n":75,"obs":0.56,"sig":false},{"hi":0.89,"lo":0.71,"mean":0.7974666666666667,"n":75,"obs":0.6133333333333333,"sig":true},{"hi":0.99,"lo":0.89,"mean":0.9405333333333336,"n":75,"obs":0.6533333333333333,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.99,"mean":0.9996536796536797,"n":231,"obs":0.8571428571428571,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":1.8,"provisional":false,"rank":176,"rank_hi":191.0,"rank_lo":132.875,"reliability":0.03154787621667454,"resolution":0.061905227952181674,"sk